&lt;p&gt;We’re proudly digital-first, giving most Upstarters the flexibility to do their best work from wherever they thrive, alongside teammates across 80+ cities in the US and Canada. Digital-first doesn’t mean distant. We’re intentional about in-person connection through team onsites, planning sessions, and moments that spark creativity and trust. And whether you choose to work primarily from home or collaborate in-person from one of our offices in Columbus, Austin, the Bay Area, or New York City, you’ll have the support to work in the way that works best for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re energized by tackling meaningful problems, excited to innovate with purpose, and motivated by work that truly matters, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team: &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s &lt;strong&gt;Partner Implementation &amp;amp; Enablement&lt;/strong&gt; team is responsible for bringing new bank and credit union partners onto our platform and keeping existing partners equipped to run their lending programs. We own the operational core of the partner relationship: the diligence materials partners use to evaluate us, the change management process that tells them when our policies and models change, and the systems that deliver both. How quickly a partner can launch, and how much confidence they have in us once they have launched, is decided by this team’s work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Diligence Program Lead&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;at Upstart, you will own the diligence and change management programs our lending partners depend on. You will answer the due diligence questionnaires that partners and their examiners require, maintain the document library and access controls behind them, and run the recurring process that notifies partners when our policies, procedures, and models change. You will work across Compliance, Lending Partnerships, Account Management, and Product to turn a set of manual, individually held processes into programs that hold up as the partner base grows.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the lending partner change management program end to end: assemble each release, notify partners of policy, procedure, and model updates, and keep the supporting document libraries current.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Respond to lending partner due diligence questionnaires and information requests, working with Compliance, Legal, and Model Risk Management to source and verify every answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain the partner-facing document repository and its access controls, including which materials each partner can reach based on their product mix and stage in the relationship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run the recurring corrective action reporting cycle: validate the source data, distribute partner-specific reports, and confirm delivery with the teams that publish them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with Product to move manual diligence and change management workflows onto supported tooling, and document each process so more than one person can run it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify gaps in policy ownership and documentation approval status, and raise them with Compliance and Lending Partnerships before they reach a partner.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualificationsu&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5 years of experience in financial services compliance, risk, audit, or third-party due diligence&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2 years of experience responding to due diligence questionnaires, regulatory examinations, or audit requests from banks, credit unions, or other regulated institutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning a recurring operational or reporting process end to end, including its documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience administering a document management system, virtual data room, or other controlled-access content repository&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of consumer lending products and the policies that govern them, including personal loans, auto, and home equity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of model risk management practices and how model documentation is shared with third parties&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of third-party risk management expectations at banks and credit unions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled in using generative AI tools to draft, verify, and maintain large volumes of written documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to build process automation in spreadsheet or workflow tools and hand it off to others to run&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to influence across compliance, legal, product, and commercial teams without direct authority&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
