&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Upstart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Upstart, we’re united by a mission that matters: to radically reduce the cost and complexity of borrowing for all Americans. Every day, we bring creativity, experimentation, and advanced AI to reshape access to credit, helping millions move forward financially with clarity and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leading AI lending marketplace, we partner with banks and credit unions to expand access to affordable credit through technology that’s both radically intelligent and deeply human. Our platform runs over one million predictions per borrower using more than 3,000 signals, powering smarter, fairer decisions for millions of customers. But the numbers only hint at the impact. Every idea, every voice, and every contribution moves us closer to a world where credit never stands between people and their financial progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proudly digital-first, giving most Upstarters the flexibility to do their best work from wherever they thrive, alongside teammates across 80+ cities in the US and Canada. Digital-first doesn’t mean distant. We’re intentional about in-person connection through team onsites, planning sessions, and moments that spark creativity and trust. And whether you choose to work primarily from home or collaborate in-person from one of our offices in Columbus, Austin, the Bay Area, or New York City, you’ll have the support to work in the way that works best for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re energized by tackling meaningful problems, excited to innovate with purpose, and motivated by work that truly matters, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help Upstart become the world’s most radically pro-consumer company in finance! As we continue building toward long-term customer trust, deeper engagement, and lifetime value, platform investments are becoming increasingly important across the customer journey. Rather than owning individual customer experiences, platform product teams develop the core capabilities that allow feature teams to innovate faster while improving reliability, scalability, and regulatory readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Principal Product Manager, Communications Platform&lt;/strong&gt;, you will drive a greenfield initiative to establish the shared communications foundation for the company. Working closely with Engineering, Compliance, Risk, and product leaders across the business, you&#39;ll define the long-term vision for how communications are delivered, orchestrated, governed, and measured across every customer touchpoint. Your work will enable product teams to deliver more personalized, trusted experiences while providing the platform capabilities, compliance guardrails, and shared infrastructure needed to support both today&#39;s products and the next generation of AI-powered customer interactions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define and execute the product strategy and roadmap&lt;/strong&gt; for Upstart&#39;s Communications Platform, balancing immediate business needs with a long-term platform vision.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Partner with engineering&lt;/strong&gt; to build shared platform capabilities, including messaging APIs, delivery infrastructure, governance controls, and communication data models that support multiple products and channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Establish scalable platform abstractions&lt;/strong&gt; that enable product teams to deliver customer communications more efficiently while reducing duplicated engineering effort.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive alignment&lt;/strong&gt; across Engineering, Growth, Servicing, Capital, Banking, Compliance, Risk, and other cross-functional partners to prioritize platform investments and influence company-wide technical strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop platform capabilities&lt;/strong&gt; that improve regulatory compliance, auditability, and operational visibility through standardized controls and monitoring.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Define success metrics&lt;/strong&gt;, evaluate platform performance, and use data and customer insights to continuously improve platform adoption, reliability, and business impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Evaluate external technologies&lt;/strong&gt; and vendor partnerships that extend platform capabilities and support future product strategy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, Statistics, Economics, or a related field (or equivalent practical experience).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience building software products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading platform, infrastructure, or developer platform products in a software organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with engineering teams to define APIs, platform capabilities, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading cross-functional product initiatives involving engineering and business stakeholders from strategy through successful delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building or scaling communications, messaging, engagement, or customer interaction platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in fintech, financial services, marketplaces, or other highly regulated industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of regulatory compliance considerations for customer communications and platform governance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to develop long-term platform strategy while balancing near-term product delivery and organizational priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience communicating technical strategy and influencing executive stakeholders across multiple organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
