&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ years experience handling regulatory escalated customer complaints within a financial institution, lending organization, or other regulated financial services environment (Consumer Financial Protection Bureau (CFPB), Better Business Bureau (BBB), State Attorney General, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting complaint investigations, documenting findings, identifying root causes, and determining or recommending customer resolutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying consumer financial regulations or requirements to complaint investigations and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of consumer financial regulations such as the Fair Credit Reporting Act (FCRA), Unfair, Deceptive, or Abusive Acts or Practices (UDAAP), Fair Debt Collection Practices Act (FDCPA), and Equal Credit Opportunity Act (ECOA).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Certified Regulatory Compliance Manager (CRCM) certification.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting auto lending or Home Equity Line of Credit (HELOC) products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze complaint data and trends to identify recurring issues and recommend operational or customer experience improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
