&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s Compliance team supports the company’s compliance management system by providing second-line oversight, guidance, and challenge across key business activities. The Compliance Advisory &amp;amp; Change Management team partners with stakeholders across the business to operationalize compliance requirements and support consistent execution of established compliance policies and procedures.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Manager, Compliance Advisory &amp;amp; Change Management at Upstart, you will help operationalize key components of Upstart’s compliance framework, with a primary focus on third-party risk management, new and modified products and services, marketing compliance, and regulatory change management. You will partner with business stakeholders to provide second-line compliance guidance, review, and challenge while maintaining clear ownership between the first and second lines of defense.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operationalize second-line compliance activities established under Upstart’s third-party risk management, new and modified products and services, marketing, and regulatory change management policies and procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review new and modified products and services for compliance considerations and provide guidance and challenge to business stakeholders throughout the applicable review process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review marketing and customer-facing materials in accordance with established compliance requirements and processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support regulatory change management by assessing relevant regulatory developments, documenting compliance impacts, and coordinating with stakeholders responsible for implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide compliance guidance and challenge related to third-party risk reviews in accordance with established third-party risk management requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and escalate material compliance concerns arising through these processes and help ensure appropriate follow-up and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
