&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Upstart&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Upstart, we’re united by a mission that matters: to radically reduce the cost and complexity of borrowing for all Americans. Every day, we bring creativity, experimentation, and advanced AI to reshape access to credit, helping millions move forward financially with clarity and confidence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the leading AI lending marketplace, we partner with banks and credit unions to expand access to affordable credit through technology that’s both radically intelligent and deeply human. Our platform runs over one million predictions per borrower using more than 3,000 signals, powering smarter, fairer decisions for millions of customers. But the numbers only hint at the impact. Every idea, every voice, and every contribution moves us closer to a world where credit never stands between people and their financial progress.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re proudly digital-first, giving most Upstarters the flexibility to do their best work from wherever they thrive, alongside teammates across 80+ cities in the US and Canada. Digital-first doesn’t mean distant. We’re intentional about in-person connection through team onsites, planning sessions, and moments that spark creativity and trust. And whether you choose to work primarily from home or collaborate in-person from one of our offices in Columbus, Austin, the Bay Area, or New York City, you’ll have the support to work in the way that works best for you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you’re energized by tackling meaningful problems, excited to innovate with purpose, and motivated by work that truly matters, we’d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Team:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s&lt;strong&gt; Digital Marketing team&lt;/strong&gt; drives scalable, data-driven customer acquisition across our lending products via performance marketing channels. We design, execute, and optimize digital media strategies that connect consumers to credit at the moments that matter most. Through rigorous experimentation, channel optimization, and disciplined CAC management, the team plays a critical role in fueling Upstart’s growth while maintaining strong unit economics for the business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the &lt;strong&gt;Senior Manager, Performance Marketing, Paid Social&lt;/strong&gt;, you will own the strategy, execution, and growth of paid social acquisition for Upstart’s Personal Loans business. You will be a hands-on media buyer responsible for building profitable scale across social platforms, partnering closely with our media agency while maintaining direct ownership of performance, testing, and optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role sits at the intersection of media buying, creative strategy, audience development, and marketing analytics. You will translate business goals into channel strategy, identify opportunities to improve conversion and efficiency, and work cross-functionally to develop the creative, targeting, and measurement capabilities needed to grow Personal Loans profitably.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role offers exceptional ownership and visibility, with the chance to make a material impact on one of Upstart’s newest and most strategic product lines while laying the foundation for long-term growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Own and optimize paid social and video acquisition&lt;/strong&gt; for Personal Loans, managing campaign strategy, setup, bidding, budgets, pacing, and performance across key platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with our media agency to&lt;strong&gt; establish channel strategy, manage execution, evaluate recommendations&lt;/strong&gt;, and hold the partnership accountable to volume, CAC, and profitability goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Be hands-on in the platform, &lt;/strong&gt;using performance data to make media investments, optimization decisions, and improve campaign efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Develop and execute a creative strategy in partnership with Creative and agency teams&lt;/strong&gt;, including testing frameworks, messaging hypotheses, formats, production priorities, and creative performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and refine audience strategies across prospecting&lt;/strong&gt;, retargeting, customer lists, lookalikes, and other first- and third-party audience solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive&amp;nbsp; geo-list targeting and geographic experimentation with our analytics team &lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to identify incremental growth opportunities, improve channel economics, and bring paid social toward profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and analyze &lt;strong&gt;structured tests across audiences, creative, bidding, placements, geographies, and funnel experiences&lt;/strong&gt;, using incrementality and down-funnel performance to guide investment decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics, Product Marketing, Creative, Lifecycle, and Growth Product teams to i&lt;strong&gt;mprove the full acquisition funnel from impression through funded loan&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and &lt;strong&gt;forecast significant media budgets&lt;/strong&gt;, balancing growth, customer volume, and contribution economics while adapting quickly to changing performance trends.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;7+ years of experience in performance marketing or digital media buying&lt;/strong&gt;, with significant hands-on experience managing paid social and video campaigns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience owning and scaling paid social acquisition programs against CAC, CPA, ROI, revenue, or profitability goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated expertise in paid social platforms, including campaign structure, bidding, budgeting, audience management, creative testing, and performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with external media agencies, including setting strategy, reviewing performance, challenging recommendations, and managing executional accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing or executing a paid media creative strategy, including messaging, format, testing, and performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills, with the ability to interpret channel and funnel data, design experiments, and make investment decisions in ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using geographic targeting, geo experiments, customer lists, or other audience segmentation approaches to improve acquisition efficiency and measure incrementality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience operating in highly regulated or longer consideration cycle vertical (e.g., financial services, fintech, lending, insurance, marketplaces).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
- Experience launching and scaling new channels or products from zero to one, with comfort operating in ambiguity and building an acquisition funnel from scratch.&lt;br&gt;- Experience working closely with product and engineering teams to improve landing pages, funnels, and on-site conversion through testing and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position location&lt;/strong&gt; This role is available in the following locations: Remote&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Time zone requirements&lt;/strong&gt; The team operates on the East/West coast time zones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel requirements&lt;/strong&gt; As a digital first company, the majority of your work can be accomplished remotely. The majority of our employees can live and work anywhere in the U.S but are encouraged to to still spend high quality time in-person collaborating via regular onsites. The in-person sessions’ cadence varies depending on the team and role; most teams meet once or twice per quarter for 2-4 consecutive days at a time.&lt;/p&gt;
