&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s Lending Operations Quality Control team plays a critical role in protecting customers, strengthening operational processes, and supporting regulatory compliance across our lending lifecycle. As a first-line-of-defense function, the team evaluates frontline activities across Onboarding, Servicing, Complaints, and Collections to identify risks, improve quality, and support bank readiness.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the Senior Operations Manager, Quality Control at Upstart, you will lead a team of five quality control professionals and help build and execute a scalable, risk-based quality control program. You’ll combine hands-on program development with people leadership, partnering across Operations, Compliance, and Risk to strengthen testing methodologies, address control gaps, and explore opportunities to improve oversight through automation and AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach, and develop a team of quality control professionals, establishing clear performance expectations, consistent calibration practices, and effective testing execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and enhance the quality control program, including risk-based testing plans, standardized review criteria, statistically sound sampling methodologies, and documentation that supports regulatory and audit readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee frontline quality reviews, including call monitoring, agent interactions, and adherence to operational procedures, to identify regulatory risks, process defects, and potential customer impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with operational leaders, Compliance, and Risk to communicate findings, identify root causes, recommend process improvements, and monitor remediation through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reporting and performance metrics that highlight quality trends, emerging risks, and opportunities to improve operational effectiveness and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with cross-functional partners to evaluate AI-enabled testing and automation capabilities, improving review coverage and efficiency while maintaining appropriate human oversight and controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Qualifications&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of experience in consumer lending operations, quality control, compliance testing, or operational risk within a regulated financial services environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly managing quality control, quality assurance, or compliance testing teams within a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing, implementing, or managing frontline operational quality control programs, including call monitoring, agent interaction reviews, or evaluations of agent adherence to established procedures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or executing sampling methodologies, standardized testing criteria, and documented quality assessments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing quality findings, root-cause analysis, corrective action tracking, or remediation monitoring within a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of consumer financial protection regulations, including UDAAP, TILA, ECOA, FCRA, FDCPA, and GLBA, and their application to lending operations.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience evaluating or implementing AI-enabled quality assurance tools, speech analytics, or automated compliance monitoring solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting bank partner oversight, regulatory examinations, or internal and external audits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to collaborate across Operations, Compliance, Risk, and technical teams to translate quality findings into sustainable process improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a fintech or evolving financial services environment, with the ability to balance regulatory expectations, operational efficiency, and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
