&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s Core Pricing team drives key initiatives that directly influence our revenue streams, unit economics, and product strategy. The team builds and evolves the common systems used to translate underwriting insights into accurate risk and profitability decisions for every loan we originate, while enabling a seamless borrower experience across products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer on Core Pricing&lt;/strong&gt;, you will design and build scalable, reliable systems that power pricing decisions across Upstart’s products. In close partnership with engineering, data science, product, and business teams, you will own meaningful technical projects, improve the architecture and reliability of our pricing services, and help translate complex modeling and business requirements into durable software capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and evolve high-performance, real-time pricing systems that support critical lending decisions across Upstart products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own complex engineering projects from technical design through delivery, balancing scalability, reliability, correctness, and speed of iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with data scientists, product managers, and business stakeholders to translate modeling and business requirements into reliable software solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement architectural improvements that increase the flexibility, maintainability, observability, and resilience of pricing services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical standards for system design, testing, monitoring, and operational excellence within the Core Pricing team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support other engineers through design reviews, technical guidance, and knowledge sharing while contributing to sound technical decisions across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
