&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, Mathematics, or a related field, or equivalent practical experience, plus 4 years of software engineering experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing, building, testing, and maintaining production backend software or services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning software engineering projects through multiple stages of the development lifecycle, from technical design through production delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or integrating APIs, services, or other components within distributed or interconnected production systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience applying software engineering practices including code review, automated testing, debugging, and production support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of identity and access management concepts and standards such as OAuth 2.0, OpenID Connect, or SAML.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working in a medium-to-large engineering organization or with systems spanning multiple engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to frontend development in addition to backend systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using AI-assisted development tools such as Cursor, Claude Code, or similar tools in software engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to learn unfamiliar technical domains, communicate technical decisions and outcomes clearly, and develop deep expertise over time.&lt;/li&gt;
