&lt;p&gt;Upstart’s Delivery team enables engineers to ship software to production safely, reliably, and with minimal friction. We build and operate the platforms and workflows that support release, deployment, production rollout, and rollback, while giving engineering teams clear visibility into what is changing and how those changes are performing.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our goal is to make software delivery predictable and self-service by creating reusable deployment capabilities, automating common operational decisions, and making the state of software in production easy to understand. We partner closely with Developer Platform, Cloud Platform, Site Reliability Engineering, Security, and product engineering teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a &lt;strong&gt;Software Engineer II, Delivery &lt;/strong&gt;at Upstart, you will build and operate the systems engineers use to release and deploy software to production. You’ll independently deliver well-scoped engineering projects, contribute to technical design, and improve the reliability and usability of systems that sit directly in the path to production.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How you’ll make an impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and improve services, automation, and developer tooling that enable engineering teams to safely release and deploy software to production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop reliable deployment capabilities, including progressive rollouts, deployment health analysis, and automated rollback, to reduce the risk of production changes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve visibility into releases, deployments, configuration, and production state so engineers can understand what changed, where it changed, and how it is performing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve the reliability, performance, observability, and usability of Delivery systems by diagnosing recurring issues and implementing durable improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Replace manual or fragmented release workflows with reusable, self-service capabilities that make the common path to production simple and consistent&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI throughout software development and problem solving, and identify opportunities for AI-enabled automation that makes software delivery safer, faster, and easier to operate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
